      "likeCount": 9,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "5e6317efd785c763f3f8223c",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Scale those default grey hidden/unoptimized avatars to the right scale based on eye level.\nOr at least make it the average VRC avatar height rather then real world height.. it's so awkward to see that huge 1.8m floating torso while the rest of the avatars are around 1.6m and lower.\nBut obviously correct height would be better.\nAnd as an even fancier goal, full body grey robots!\nAnd even fancier just custom for each player!!",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Scale performance grey robots",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5b7f61f7c344422f90eb286e",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 33
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Note: this is about automatically \"blocked\" avatars due to performance, not avatar people hide manually.\nWould be nice if we would be allowed to provide fallback avatars too... just like you can upload avatar that is different on quest/pc. It would be nice to be able to upload simplified version of avatar for people using performance limit options.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
